  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own multi-year 'Key operating and financial data' summary table (audited), cross-validated against the Balance Sheet wherever available. This bank has operated with deeply negative shareholders' equity and a deeply negative Capital Adequacy Ratio (CAR) throughout the entire researched period (2013-2024), i.e. it has been technically insolvent by conventional accounting/regulatory measures for over a decade — a legacy of the 2006 collapse and nationalization of its predecessor, The Oriental Bank Limited, on fraud/mismanagement grounds. As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investments' rather than 'NPL'. Sourced from this bank's own FY2013 annual report (a differently-re-sourced capture than the rest of this dataset; see sources.json), which is more precise than the FY2017 report's retrospective 5-year table used for FY2014-2015 (that table's FY2013 CAR of -89.97% vs this primary source's -89.81% is a minor cross-report rounding difference). Total equity here uses Tier-I core capital, verified equal to paid-up capital + statutory reserve + general reserve + retained earnings for this institution (see FY2012 note).",
